'''Fractured items''' are of a special type of [[item]] base that have at least one affix coloured in gold ({{c|fractured|◼}}) that is permanently fixed on the item. Items with fractured mod(s) can be dropped from rare monsters, rewards from various content, or created via using a [[Fracturing Orb]].

==How to obtain==
* {{c|magic|Magic}} items that drop Unidentified with Tier 5 rarity have a chance to have a fractured modifier.
* Players can turn a non-influenced, non-synthesized, and non-fractured rare item with at least 4 modifiers into a fractured item using a {{il|Fracturing Orb}}.
* [[Beastcrafting]] has crafting options that fracture one or two modifiers on a rare [[talisman]].
* A {{il|Fractured Fossil}} causes the resulting item to have a fractured modifier.
* The [[Azurite Mine]] contains nodes that can drop items with Delve-specific drop-only modifiers. Since [[version 3.16.0]], items with those drop-only modifiers have a chance to be fractured.
* {{psl|Pillage and Plunder}} causes [[Immortal Syndicate]] members to have a chance to drop an item with a fractured [[veiled mod]].

===Legacy methods===
* [[The Necropolis|Necropolis]] crafting can use a {{c|mod|#% chance to Fracture an explicit modifier}} corpse modifier to create fractured items. With over 100% chance, this can be used to create an item with multiple fractured mods.
* [[Breachlord]]s in Flawless [[Breachstone]]s have a chance to drop a {{il|Grasping Mail}} with a random fractured Breach mod.
* The unique [[Vaal side area]] [[Grand Dreams]] dropped an item with a fractured [[Incursion modifier]].

Other sources of regular fractured items included Exceptional Rogue Exiles from {{il|Horned Scarab of Awakening}}, [[monster modifier]] reward loot conversion, [[The Genesis Tree]], and certain Maven's Invitations.

==Mechanics==
* Fractured items have their own symbol before and after the item name: [[File:Fractured-item-symbol.png]].
* Fractured items have at least one permanent "Fractured" mod. These mods cannot be removed (by {{il|Orb of Annulment}} or {{il|Orb of Scouring}}, etc.) or have its values changed by {{il|Divine Orb}}. The mod text is gold in colour.
** Most fractured items will have one fractured modifier, dropped or crafted. The exception to this is the [[beastcrafting]] recipe that uses a [[Fenumal Plagued Arachnid]] and [[The Black Mórrígan]] to fracture two modifiers on a rare [[talisman]].
** There is technically no hard limit on the number of fractured mods an item can have. It was possible to obtain an item with up to three fractured mods in [[Synthesis league]], and [[Necropolis league]] allowed items with up to six fractured modifiers to be crafted.
* When using an {{il|Orb of Scouring}} on a fractured item, it will turn into a Magic item if it had one fractured mod or a Rare item if it had two or three fractured mods. For crafting purposes, players could create a Rare item with one fractured affix by using a {{il|Regal Orb}} then an {{il|Orb of Annulment}}.
* Fractured items cannot be turned into [[unique item]]s with an {{il|Orb of Chance}}.
* Fractured items cannot be turned into an [[influenced item]]. [[Influenced Exalted Orb]]s and {{il|Awakener's Orb|Awakener's Orbs}} cannot be used on them. Conversely, influenced items cannot be turned into a fractured item.
** It was possible to create a fractured influenced item in [[Necropolis league]] via [[The Necropolis|Necropolis]] crafting. 
* [[Synthesised item]] cannot be fractured.
* Fractured items cannot have [[Imprint]]s made of them or applied to them.

==Unique fractured items==
Unique fractured items could only be acquired during [[Synthesis league]] and cannot be chanced from a fractured basetype. Players can now acquire those items from trading with other players in permanent leagues only.
