==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.30.0|
* Tier 5 items have a chance to drop as Fractured Magic items.
* Removed many sources of Fractured Items dropping, primarily from League Mechanics such as Legion, Ritual, Heist, Blight, Delirium, Delve and Incursion.
* Removed the random Rare monster modifier conversion for all Items dropping as Fractured.
* Disabled Expedition Remnants that cause Excavated chests and Runic monsters to drop Fractured Items.
* Removed the Solid Cysts]] Notable Passive from the Genesis Tree Equipment subtree.
* Exceptional Rogue Exiles no longer have a chance to drop all items Fractured.
* Lowered the chance for Delve specific Rare item Modifiers to be Fractured.
* The Forgotten and The Feared Maven Invitations no longer drop bonus Fractured rare items.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.20.0|
* Introduced {{il|Fracturing Orb}}, and removed the [[Harvest crafting|Harvest Craft]] that fractures a random modifier on an item.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.19.1b|
* Flasks can now have Fractured modifiers, which can be obtained through the Empowered Elements conversion modifier.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.19.0e|
* The Harvest craft that fractures a random modifier on an item with at least 5 modifiers can now be used on an item with at least 4 modifiers.
* Fracture a random modifier on an item with at least 4 modifiers, locking it in place now has a cost of 10000 (previously 50000).
}}
{{Version history table row|3.19.0|
* Harvest monsters are no longer associated with specific crafting options and do not grant uses of crafting options on death. Instead, monsters defeated now drop a stack of lifeforce.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.16.0|
* Now also drops from [[Azurite Mine]].<ref name="Azurite Mine" />
}}
{{Version history table row|3.13.0|
* Imprinted {{il|Eternal Orb|Eternal Orbs}} can no longer be applied to '''Fractured items''', overriding their Fractured modifiers.
* Harvest rewards can no longer appear in Heists, because Harvest is a thing again.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.12.0|
* Now as a drop in [[Heist]]. {{Undocumented}}
}}
{{Version history table row|3.11.0|
* Now can fracture a mod on existing items in [[Harvest league]].<ref name=Harvest/>
}}
{{Version history table row|3.8.0|
* If you're lucky, Zana will now offer 5 new unique maps as part of her missions. Each map contains a boss encounter originally from the Synthesis league, and each can drop unique items originally exclusive to that league. Note, you cannot obtain Fractured items, nor will you have any access to the Synthesiser.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.6.3|
* Fractured Items now drop from all Memory Nexus areas, rather than just Decaying areas.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.6.0|
* Introduced to the game as league-specific items.
}}
{{Version history table end}}

